  "canonical_form": {
    "description": "Rules for producing a deterministic token from the same input.",
    "rules": [
      "Peaks sorted m/z-ascending before encoding; all parallel arrays (incl. auxiliary) permuted identically.",
      "NaN and Inf values are not allowed in any float array.",
      "Array descriptors emitted in fixed order: m/z, intensity, charge, ion mobility, then auxiliary arrays sorted ascending by key (CV accession string, or name for non-standard arrays).",
      "Integrity hash (optional third token part) is computed over the ASCII text of the first two token parts, 'magic.payload' (blobs are inline in the payload and therefore covered).",
      "Hash algorithm: SHA-256, first 12 bytes, base64url-encoded (16 chars).",
      "Numpress fp is a whole number. Defaults: linear 100000; slof floor(min(3600, 65535/ln(max+1))), clamped DOWN so no encoded value overflows uint16. A descriptor omits fp when it equals the default and carries the clamped value otherwise.",
      "Arrays containing negative values fall back to the lossless zlib codec in lossy mode (numpress cannot represent them); negative m/z is rejected."
    ]
  }
}